## Gates

Authoritative check: `python3 tools/gate_lint.py MASTER_GAME.md` (or the game directory).
The Status column is a claim. gate-lint recomputes every D-* gate from the numbers
above and does not trust this column. Generalistic rows are flavor. human_touch is
`leave`, `optional`, `suggested`, or `blocked`. Creative fill must not break a D-* gate.

### Deterministic
| Gate ID | Check | Value | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| D-MAP-01 | room_count >= 2 | <n> | unchecked |
| D-MAP-02 | meters; grow toward -Z; x = 0 is the center line | <units, axis> | unchecked |
| D-MAP-03 | beginner floor_y is 0.0 | <floor_y list> | unchecked |
| D-ROOM-01 | snake_case room id, unique | <ids> | unchecked |
| D-ROOM-02 | width >= 4 m and depth >= 4 m | <sizes> | unchecked |
| D-ROOM-03 | room interiors do not overlap | <centers> | unchecked |
| D-ROOM-04 | height >= 2.5 m (default 3.0) | <heights> | unchecked |
| D-EXIT-01 | start has a forward exit; goal has an entry; transit has two | <exit counts> | unchecked |
| D-EXIT-02 | door or open sides meet on a shared edge | <which doors meet> | unchecked |
| D-EXIT-03 | start reaches goal through those doors | <path> | unchecked |
| D-START-01 | start_room_id names a room | <id> | unchecked |
| D-START-02 | start point inside the start room, inset >= 0.75 m | <pos or auto> | unchecked |
| D-GOAL-01 | goal_room_id names a room | <id> | unchecked |
| D-GOAL-02 | win is all_grunts_down | all_grunts_down | unchecked |
| D-ENEMY-01 | at least one grunt | <count> | unchecked |
| D-ENEMY-02 | grunt inside its room; one grunt in the goal or on the path | <id in room> | unchecked |
| D-ITEM-01 | pickups, if any, sit inside their room | <id in room or none> | unchecked |
| D-PAL-01 | every room color names a palette entry | <color keys> | unchecked |
| D-ID-01 | piece, enemy, and item ids are unique snake_case | ids unique | unchecked |
| D-SAFE-01 | target_map is fresh_demo | fresh_demo | unchecked |

